    "notes": [
      "The operator separately publishes a combined-circuit map in its public media catalogue. It identifies a northern-straight exit curving south along the western side of the paddock and a western connecting branch between the northern return diagonal and the southern inner U. That map supplies branch identity only and is not georeferenced, digitized or redistributed. The track-page combined graphic duplicates the southern circuit and remains excluded. All coordinates are independently digitized from the pinned September 2026 Copernicus raster, with June native red, green, blue and near-infrared bands corroborating both connectors. The route retains the northern outer loop and inner western U, upper chicane, northeastern hairpin, eastern paddock-side connection, southern eastern return, long southern straight, western southern hairpin and complete inner spiral. It omits the standalone northern middle S and standalone southern outer northern cap, as identified by the combined-course map. The existing independent southern public road snapshot corroborates pavement identity; no source vertices are moved to a supplied timing point or nominal distance. Native resolution is 10 m. Fine corner radii, centerline placement, direction and historical equivalence remain draft. The independent measured distance is preserved. This is a coarse supporting course trace, not a certified timed lap. No supplied boundary coordinates or diagram pixels supply geometry. Independently digitized aerial centerline: 7011.3 m. Direction, historical configuration and fine corner alignment remain draft; no course coordinates come from the comparison catalogue."
    ]
